## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE; apply it)
*Blocker:* a wrong money figure (against your hand derivation: a fixed or manual line counted as anything but its typed quantity, a per-device line changed, a tier, fee, device count or deal figure off its derivation); a CHANGED pre-existing figure or member, or a no-rule or stated-`PerDevice` result or input that differs from main AT ALL under any of the three serializers (the B980-1 class); a changed InputHash for a stored-shape input, or a stated `PerDevice` whose hash differs from unset; `quantityRule` serialised at the default; an undefined rule that prices by any route; an exception at head on a quote that priced at main; an Api src, contract, `docs/api`, `docs/API.md`, web, rental, `QuoteInput.cs`, `QuoteCalculator.cs`, `InputHash.cs`, `WorkbookRules.cs`, workflow, `Directory.Build.props` or csproj byte; `PurchaseEngineVersion` changed; a path beyond the 6; a removed existing test line; a string literal in `src/` beyond the three words; the head moved (a verdict is valid only at the head it ran on); a secret; a build warning; a reproduced failing test at head and not at main (run alone 3 times); **a head-written stored record that MAIN's binary refuses under the store options.** *Major (class):* a reconciler that agrees with a wrong price or disagrees with a right one beyond X-34's named limit (the B1009-1 class: a quote that reconciles at main and disagrees at head only because a rule was stated); a `FixedPerGroup` and a `Manual` line differing in any figure; a non-group section whose figures differ from its unset twin; a survivor of step 6's closed list; an X-35, X-40, X-41, X-42, comment or commit-message sentence FALSE against your measurement; a builder claim contradicted with a verdict consequence (555/193/3,165, 35,658, 40 of 40, 20 of 20, 78 of 78, 6 of 6 tamper rows, "lost 0 added 50"); a hard clause of the acceptance NOT MET. *Minor/Note:* a register sentence SHORT, not FALSE (including X-40's `perSite`/`usageOnly` sentence if only by-name is a deserialisation error); the REAL store and Api options not pinned by a committed row (builder Correction 3) when you measure them equal; X-34's reconciler limit named and not pinned by a row; a mutant killed by the sweep alone, or `n2`/`o3`/`l2` unprotected by a builder mutant when your mutant is killed by their rows; the `PerDevice` red-first reading (a reading for the product owner, Note unless NO row of the build kills a PerDevice-ignoring mutant, then Major); the spelling gap between the ticket's `fixedPerGroup` and the stored `FixedPerGroup`; the builder's prediction misses (MQ7, MQ16 under-listed), its process slips (a `cd`, its first harness form) and its "20 of 22" count if true; unsigned commit; the known timing rows; CodeQL and hosted CI NOT RUN (no PR); Linux, node 24 and the python job you cannot run. Say which rule you applied for every finding, and give every finding a fix-shape in prose. Round 1 of 2: do not pad a Note into a NO GO and do not soften a Blocker or a Major: quote the row, the input, the expected figure, the observed figure. A security-shaped finding you cannot classify is a STOP.
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs steps 1-8 measured with controls, c0 and c1 green, c-fail met, your hand cases green at head and red under their mutants, BYTE-EQUAL rebuilt by you with every pre-existing member equal to main under all three serializers, the stored-quote reading of 1(d) done with the rollback read, the sweep at 0 differences with a control that can see a difference, the reconciler tamper rows not agreeing, the local CI line green, every NOT RUN named. GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note only (say "NO PR; hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN" on the line above the verdict line). NO GO on any Blocker or Major, with the class named, "round 1 of 2", and the fix-shape in prose (a second NO GO on this class closes it and goes to the product owner). **THE SWEEP (binding, your own, in the harness):** at least 500 quotes (`new Random(seed)`, synthetic), generator shape stated as a PROPERTY first: each line's rule from {unset, stated `PerDevice`, `FixedPerGroup`, `Manual`}, groups N unset and 0..6 plus a few large, q 0..9, manual items, book devices and options, optional, credit, included, override, markup and margin methods, fees on either side, section rates with and without a supplies model or a deal usage with and without one, `FleetTotal` lines, every allowed term, and a share of blocked quotes (an undefined rule 99, -1, 3, 4; a negative quantity); at least these, then any other shape the harness suites hold: prove it meets the property or STOP; print the census per class. For each quote: (i) counted quantity and line cost, margin and sell equal YOUR independent formula from the INPUT (the rule table) and the unit figures the result recorded; section totals by X-21; device quantity, device count, tier, fee and deal figures; exact; (ii) metamorphic: where every fixed or manual q is divisible by N above 0, the per-device twin (q / N) is equal in every figure beyond the two line keys (print how many qualified); (iii) a quote with every rule unset or `PerDevice` is raw-equal to base under three serializers and its twin with the rule removed is equal; (iv) `quantityPerDevice` and `quantityRule` present exactly as the rule table says, by path; (v) `Reconcile` agrees on 100 percent of priced quotes or the disagreement is X-34's stated limit and the same quote with every rule removed disagrees likewise; (vi) 0 exceptions beyond base's and every undefined rule blocked. Control that can fail: the sweep run on your GQ1, GQ2 and GQ8 must report differences, else its zero is NOT EVIDENCE. **First line of STATUS (placeholder at Step 0 `GATE VERDICT B1075: PENDING`; verdict form, ONE line):** `GATE VERDICT B1075: branch b1062/mps-253-component-quantity-rules <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ 8d6a6b5 on main 3496da3 (round 1 of 2 on class "V4 engine: component quantity rules", NO GO 0 before; NO PR, hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN - delta <1 commit, 6 paths, +<a> -<r>; HOLDS bytes n; test lines removed n; ci.yml blob = main y/n; PurchaseEngineVersion unchanged y/n; X-40 to X-42 present y/n, sentences true n of N, X-35 sentences false n short n; new literals n (the three y/n)> - names <Engine 505/555, Import 193/193, Api 3165/3165; lost n added n> - arithmetic <fixed and manual q not 1 not N y/n; N 1 y/n; N 0 y/n; large N y/n; mixed group y/n; non-group equals unset y/n; metamorphic y/n; decimals exact y/n; tier pool y/n; deal usage y/n; fleet total y/n; fee x N y/n; supplies k own y/n; reconciler agrees y/n; tamper rows not agreeing n of n; X-34 limit pinned by a row y/n> - readings <N 0 keeps a fixed charge measured y/n, graded as built y/n; tier pool as typed measured y/n, graded as built y/n> - refusal <integer n of n; name n of n; serialised integer n of n; path y/n; words n listed; reachable by a caller n> - BYTE-EQUAL <files n; InputHash options differing n of n, ApiJson n of n, store n of n; no-rule and PerDevice raw-equal y/n; key paths n; InputHash n of 40, PerDevice n of 20; rollback read y/n; control n> - sweep <n quotes; differences n; metamorphic n; exceptions n; reconciler disagreements n (limit n); control sees a difference y/n> - mutants <c0, c1; GQ n of 34; survivors n; sweep-only n; n2 o3 l2 killed n; c-fail y/n> - CI local <e/i/a, failed n skipped n warnings n, TMPDIR outside git y/n; web and python NOT RUN by reason> - merge <conflicts n; shared paths n> - commit sentences true n of N - gitleaks rc <n> - squash files checked y/n, no NOT TESTED line y/n)`. Last line exactly one of `VERDICT: B1075 branch b1062/mps-253-component-quantity-rules @ 8d6a6b5 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (round 1 of 2) on main 3496da3` (finding ids with severities, the class and "NO PR; hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN" on the line above it; the line carries no landing word) or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`. **LANDING HOLD (Tuesday's, never yours):** after a GO or GO WITH FINDINGS, Tuesday opens the PR from the branch, reads the hosted checks and alerts at the same head, and lands the SAME commit through CodeQL with the head pinned and your explicit subject and body; no bypass, nothing deployed. **STATUS-NOW:** write STATUS at Step 0 with the placeholder first line and a moving `WORKING: <part> <time>` last line; update after every check, marking superseded lines `(superseded by <section>)`; RESUME at about 80 percent of context or at the hard stop (`## PROGRESS and RESUME`: done/partial per step, next exact commands, every tree and mutant with restore proof; end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY continue in a fresh seat from RESUME`). **CLOCK:** every time you write in STATUS is the output of a `date` call made at that moment (the Step-0 line, each `WORKING:` line, the verdict time, the lock and slot holders); the target (3 hours) and the hard stop (5 hours) are written at Step 0 as durations after the Step-0 `date` and as absolute clocks computed from it by `date -v+3H` and `date -v+5H`, labelled PLAN; the verdict time is a fresh `date`, never the plan.
**FOR TUESDAY (what STATUS carries).** The verdict in words with class and round; the rule in one paragraph (the counted quantity per rule, N 0, N 1, large N, non-group, the carried members, the refusal); the arithmetic table of step 2 with your hand-derived literals and the observed figures; the two readings of step 3, each in plain words with the figures under it and under its alternative, for the product owner; the BYTE-EQUAL, hash and sweep figures; the stored-quote reading in plain words (what a stored quote holds, whether a rollback reads it, that an Api-made quote gains nothing and why); the refusal table of step 4 and the three words ready to copy for the words gate with "no caller reaches them today" and its proof; the mutant table in one paragraph; the commit message with each sentence carried or NOT carried; X-35, X-40, X-41, X-42 and the comments each judged; the Done-when table with the `PerDevice` red-first judgment, the two records sentences and, for each unowned item, what a records seat should file; the squash subject and body (four files) and the exact merge line; stale or false statements in the builder STATUS; what changes if main moves first; the LANDING CHECKLIST.
